The 128K limit lives in the **pi harness code**, not the model:

```javascript
// /usr/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist/core/model-registry.js:461
contextWindow: modelDef.contextWindow ?? 128000,
```

If pi doesn't know your model's actual context window, it falls back to **128,000 tokens** hardcoded. That means it will start compacting/summarizing context at that point, even though the underlying model could handle 1M.

**Fix it by declaring the real `contextWindow` in your pi config.** Edit `~/.pi/agent/models.json`:

**If it's a custom provider/model:**
```json
{
  "providers": {
    "my-provider": {
      "models": [
        {
          "id": "your-1m-model",
          "contextWindow": 1000000
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

**If it's a built-in provider/model, use an override:**
```json
{
  "providers": {
    "openai": {
      "modelOverrides": {
        "gpt-4o-whatever": {
          "contextWindow": 1000000
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Then run `/model` (or restart the session) so pi reloads the config. From that point, the harness will budget and compact based on your declared 1M window instead of the 128K fallback.

